<title>GERMANY: TABLE-OECD German deficit forecasts for 1997, 1998.</title>
<headline>TABLE-OECD German deficit forecasts for 1997, 1998.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris-based Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development published the following forecasts for German public sector financial balances on Tuesday.</p>
<p>						 1996     1997     1998</p>
<p> General government		     -134.0   -118.3   -101.6</p>
<p>   (percentage of GDP		   -3.8     -3.2     -2.7</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>  Territorial authorities	     -120.0   -114.0   -100.0</p>
<p>  Federal government		    -78.5    -76.0    -66.0</p>
<p> National accounts adjustments	-0.8     -2.3     -2.6</p>
<p> Social security			  -13.1    -2.0	1.0</p>
<p> Extended public sector		 -134.0   -118.3   -101.6</p>
<p>   (percentage of GDP		   -3.8     -3.2     -2.7</p>
<p>   (cyclically adjusted pct of GDP  -3.1     -2.6     -2.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures, except percentage figures, in billions of</p>
<p>marks.</p>
<p>--Janet Northcote, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
